s) are a type of recurrent neural network used for processing time-series data. They consist of a large, fixed-size, randomly connected hidden layer called the \"reservoir\" that processes input data. The weights of the reservoir are typically fixed, and only the output weights are trained. Training in ESNs is often done using simple linear regression on the reservoir's activations.\n\nSummarizing the arXiv papers:\n1. \"Integer Echo State Networks: Efficient Reservoir Computing for Digital Hardware\" - Discusses the application of ESNs in digital hardware for efficient computation.\n2. \"Evolutionary Echo State Network: evolving reservoirs in the Fourier space\" - Focuses on evolving ESNs in the Fourier domain for improved performance.\n\nBoth papers explore different aspects of ESNs, with one emphasizing hardware efficiency and the other on evolutionary methods.","role":"assistant"},"model":"qwen2.5:7b","prompt_eval_count":773,"prompt_eval_duration":249047000,"total_duration":2284678600}}